% SCAFFOLDING stand-in for SIMPOS's class `network_listener_buffer`,
% compiled by psi/espc.py into the package `simpos`.  It is NOT SIMPOS: no
% part of it is printed or held.  It is MINIMAL: only create/4, whose two
% integer arguments are kept but whose meaning is UNKNOWN.  INTERPOLATED
% (labelled) from:
%   - gog-kl1 ESP/COMMU.ESP:124-135 (ICOT Free Software, IFS
%     exper-apps/pimos/gog-kl1.tar.Z; docs/simpos/subsystems/notes/
%     fixpoint_fe.tsv:137-139): `:create(#network_listener_buffer, Sb, 16,
%     16)`, then `:set_send_data_size(Sb, 20)` and `:data_buffer(Sb, Ss)`,
%     a string the program writes with set_substring/4 and sends;
%   - pimfep's buffer/2 methods (as_pimos_login_requester,
%     pimos_login_requester, pimos_remote_login_server and _replier) and
%     sline_scsi_stream create/4 (held .ptf): `:create(#network_listener_
%     buffer, Buf, 2, 16)` (`a7 01 00 02`, `a7 02 00 10`) and `(Buf, 16250,
%     32)` (`a7 01 3f 7a`, `a7 02 00 20`), then `:set_buffer(Self, Buf)`.
% Not stood in: data_buffer/2, set_send_data_size/2, buffer/3, convert/7
% (required/classes.tsv): what the integers size is not settled by any
% held text.  They stay UNKNOWN.  INFERENCE, with sources: the first is
% a length in elements and the second the element width in bits (an ESP
% string element is 1, 8, 16 or 32 bits wide, TM-388 PDF p29): kappa2
% kernel/net/SRVCMD.ESP:22 creates `(..,2048,16)`, and 2048 x 16 bits
% = 4096 bytes, the "length = 4096 byte (double_bytes string)" buffer of
% kappa2 kernel/net/MSGCMD.ESP:22 (made by `:buffer(Class,Buffer,4096)`
% at :38-39).

class network_listener_buffer has

% INTERPOLATED from: the call sites above: the buffer comes back in the
% first argument after the class.  OURS: the two integers are kept, their
% meaning UNKNOWN.
:create(Class, Buffer, First, Second) :-
        :new(Class, Buffer),
        Buffer!first_argument := First,
        Buffer!second_argument := Second;

instance

% INTERPOLATED: the representation (OURS).
attribute first_argument := 0, second_argument := 0;

end.
